# SHA-256 checksums of the archive fetched by scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.sh for
# each supported platform. Format: "<sha256>  <goos>_<goarch>".
#
# Bump these together with any URL change in fetch-ffmpeg.sh. To recompute:
#   curl -fsSL <URL> | sha256sum
# (or `shasum -a 256` on macOS).
#
# Provenance:
#   linux_*  : johnvansickle.com  ffmpeg 7.0.2 release static (Aug 2024)
#              <https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/releases/>
#   darwin_amd64  : evermeet.cx  ffmpeg 7.1 (Sep 2024)
#                   <https://evermeet.cx/ffmpeg/>
#   darwin_arm64  : osxexperts.net  ffmpeg 7.1 arm64 (Oct 2024)
#                   <https://www.osxexperts.net/>
#   windows_amd64 : BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds  win64-lgpl static (latest tag)
#                   <https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases>
#
# License posture: johnvansickle/evermeet/osxexperts ship GPL builds
# (they include libx264/libx265). BtbN's "lgpl" variant strips those out.
# The simulator runs ffmpeg as a fork+exec subprocess, which FFmpeg's own
# legal.html treats as a separate program — so even a GPL ffmpeg blob
# does not contaminate our MIT-licensed Go binary. See scripts/ffmpeg-build.md.

